{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03QQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$G$", "MATH_0002": "$G$", "MATH_0003": "$G$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-equivalence-sheaves-point}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a57c579fe57d67c19c3df2c90badd86d3da5b63a42b985a91f1a245b7af5fcf7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:006c16afb3e8c7631653af1c2552f39897c317ae78c349ed81e5222bcfeab721", "source_text": "In\nTheorem <REF_0001>\nwe have seen the equivalence between sheaves of sets and <MATH_0001>-sets.\nThe current lemma follows formally from this as an abelian sheaf is just\na sheaf of sets endowed with a commutative group law, and a <MATH_0002>-module\nis just a <MATH_0003>-set endowed with a commutative group law.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b89484a3f17849ff9b35b57c8de900c8e595393a47abfe9fd41122bf96874f6f", "unit_id": "tag:04JQ:proof"}
